This library is an original implementation. It is not a port or derivative of
ImageMagick, and contains no ImageMagick code. ImageMagick is used only by the
optional benchmark harness in test/harness/, which shells out to the `magick`
executable to decode images and to produce comparison baselines. ImageMagick is
distributed under the ImageMagick License (Apache-2.0 style); see
https://imagemagick.org/script/license.php

Algorithm provenance
--------------------

Colour quantisation by variance minimisation:
    Xiaolin Wu, "Efficient Statistical Computations for Optimal Color
    Quantization", Graphics Gems II, Academic Press, 1991, pp. 126-133.

Iterative centroid refinement (k-means / Lloyd's algorithm):
    S. P. Lloyd, "Least squares quantization in PCM", IEEE Transactions on
    Information Theory, vol. 28, no. 2, pp. 129-137, 1982.

Error-diffusion dithering:
    R. W. Floyd and L. Steinberg, "An adaptive algorithm for spatial greyscale",
    Proceedings of the Society for Information Display, vol. 17, no. 2,
    pp. 75-77, 1976.

Space-filling-curve dithering:
    Thiadmer Riemersma, "A Balanced Dithering Technique", C/C++ Users Journal,
    December 1998.

Hilbert curve index-to-coordinate conversion:
    The standard iterative formulation, as described in
    "Programming the Hilbert curve" (J. Skilling, 2004) and widely published.

Ordered dithering matrix:
    B. E. Bayer, "An optimum method for two-level rendition of continuous-tone
    pictures", IEEE International Conference on Communications, 1973.

Perceptual colour space:
    Björn Ottosson, "A perceptual color space for image processing" (OkLab),
    2020. https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/
    Published by the author into the public domain / under the MIT license.

sRGB transfer function:
    IEC 61966-2-1:1999.
